body:
The issue is that both `ConfigService` and `Router` are eager providers which are initialized during `Injector.createInternal()`:

```ts
AppModuleInjector.prototype.createInternal = function() {
  var self = this;
  //...
  // 1. The injector is not fully initialized when the ConfigService is created
  self._ConfigService_4 = new jit_ConfigService37(self);
  // ...
  // 2. the router is not only initialized after
  self._Router_20 = jit_setupRouter59(self._ApplicationRef_8,self._UrlSerializer_12,self._RouterOutletMap_13,self._Location_16,self,self._NgModuleFactoryLoader_18,self._Compiler_17,self._InjectionToken_ROUTES_19,self._InjectionToken_ROUTER_CONFIGURATION_14,self.parent.get(jit_UrlHandlingStrategy60,null),self.parent.get(jit_RouteReuseStrategy61,null));

}
```

`injector.get(Router)` is called in the constructor of `ConfigService` before the router service gas been created.

The returned value is then `undefined` as the injector provides the `Router` but it has not been initialized yet.

Notes:
- This issue is not related to the `Router` but is a more general issue,
- Because more providers are eager now it is more likely to happen,
- We will work to fix this issue.

I was blocked also but was able to work around this issue with AOT by following https://github.com/angular/angular-cli/issues/5762#issuecomment-295670906. Injecting the injector into my service used with APP_INITIALIZER and waiting for it to be initialized. 

import { LOCATION_INITIALIZED } from '@angular/common';
import { Injectable, Injector } from '@angular/core';
import { Http } from '@angular/http';

// Services
import { AnalyticsService } from './services/analytics.service';
import { SettingsService } from './services/settings.service';

@Injectable()
export class AppConfigService {
	private isInit = false;

	/**
	 * Creates an instance of AppConfigService.
	 * @param {Injector} injector - angular injector
	 * @param {SettingsService} settingsService - service used to load config from server
	 * @param {Http} http - angular http
	 * @param {AnalyticsService} analyticsService - Injected here to instantiate only
	 *
	 * @memberOf AppConfigService
	 */
	constructor(
		private injector: Injector,
		private settingsService: SettingsService,
		private http: Http,
		private analyticsService: AnalyticsService) {}

	// Initializes the settings service with data from server as app starts
	load(): boolean|Promise<boolean> {
		const p: Promise<any> = this.injector.get(LOCATION_INITIALIZED, Promise.resolve(null));
		return p.then(() => {
			if (!this.isInit) {
				return this.settingsService.init();
			} else {
				return true;
			}
		});
	}
}

