I'm having trouble getting the loader to work with IE11, 

> ERROR TypeError: Unable to get property 'get' of undefined or null reference

Stepping through it reveals that `this.http` is undefined [here](https://github.com/ngx-translate/http-loader/blob/master/src/http-loader.ts#L14):

    TranslateHttpLoader.prototype.getTranslation = function (lang) {
        return this.http.get("" + this.prefix + lang + this.suffix)
            .map(function (res) { return res.json(); });
    };

The same code works fine for half my team, suggesting that it's a race condition. I suspect that it's related to https://github.com/angular/angular/issues/15501 (which I found after reading through [this issue](https://github.com/angular/angular-cli/issues/5762#issuecomment-295670906)), but I'm not sure.
